---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Blanc Spaces | Blanc Browser"
  description="Save a window’s tabs and groups as a space, free. Switch sets in place and return after relaunch, with everything stored locally."
  path="/features/workspaces"
  page="feature-workspaces"
  current="features"
  ogImage="/feature-workspaces.png"
  ogImageAlt="Blanc’s Spaces menu open below the Island, listing Work, Home, Painting class and Lisbon trip."
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline slot="head">
{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://blanc.day/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Features","item":"https://blanc.day/features"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"Blanc Spaces","item":"https://blanc.day/features/workspaces"}]}
  </script>
<main id="main-content" class="feature-page feature-detail-page">
  <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/features">features</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">blanc spaces</span></nav>
  <section class="feature-hero feature-hero--detail feature-hero--text" aria-labelledby="workspaces-title">
    <p class="section-kicker">Blanc Spaces</p>
    <h1 id="workspaces-title">Work, home and side projects, each in its own space.</h1>
    <p>When one window holds everything, tabs pile up and get in each other’s way. Give each part of your day its own space, then switch from the Island. Its tabs and groups come back, even after you restart.</p>
  </section>
  <figure class="product-capture feature-capture released-capture">
    <a href="/feature-captures/workspaces-v1.33.0.png" aria-label="View full Blanc Spaces capture"><img src="/feature-captures/workspaces-v1.33.0.webp" width="1440" height="900" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Blanc in the Painting class space on The Met’s Wheat Field with Cypresses page, with the Spaces menu open below the Island listing Work, Home, Painting class and Lisbon trip, each with its colour and symbol." /></a>
    <figcaption>Switch spaces from the Island.</figcaption>
  </figure>
  <section class="feature-copy-grid feature-copy-grid--top" aria-labelledby="workspaces-section-0">
    <div><h2 id="workspaces-section-0">Name it once. Keep it up to date as you browse.</h2></div>
    <div class="feature-copy-list">
      <article><h3>Save this window or start a new set</h3><p>Open the space control in the command panel or type /space. Anyone can save the current window or create a blank space.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Bring your Spaces from Arc</h3><p>In Bring Your Tabs (type /bring-tabs), choose Arc, and each Space you pick becomes a space here, with its pinned tabs, its Today tabs and its folders as tab groups. <a href="/arc-alternative">Switching from Arc</a></p></article>
      <article><h3>Return without rebuilding the set</h3><p>A bound space automatically saves its tabs and groups as you browse and returns after relaunch. Switching replaces the current window’s set; a space already open elsewhere brings that window forward.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Tell spaces apart at a glance</h3><p>Give each space a colour and a symbol. The current space shows at the start of the Island; click it to switch, edit, reorder or delete a space, with Undo.</p></article>
      <article><h3>You decide what belongs together</h3><p>Create groups and assign tabs yourself. Blanc saves those choices; it does not detect tasks or organize tabs by meaning.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <figure class="product-capture feature-capture released-capture">
    <a href="/feature-captures/workspaces-edit-v1.33.0.png" aria-label="View full Blanc Spaces editor capture"><img src="/feature-captures/workspaces-edit-v1.33.0.webp" width="1440" height="900" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="The Painting class space’s editor below the Island: its name, eight colour swatches with purple selected, and sixteen symbols with the graduation cap selected." /></a>
    <figcaption>Give each space a colour and a symbol.</figcaption>
  </figure>
  <section class="feature-copy-grid" aria-labelledby="workspaces-section-1">
    <div><h2 id="workspaces-section-1">Free, on every desktop platform.</h2></div>
    <div class="feature-copy-list">
      <article><h3>Available on every desktop platform</h3><p>Blanc Spaces is free for everyone on macOS, Windows and Linux. Blanc Patron is an optional subscription that supports Blanc’s development; it doesn’t unlock any feature.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Existing spaces remain yours</h3><p>Your spaces stay on this device, in this profile, and keep updating as you browse. Nothing about them depends on a subscription.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Keep private browsing separate</h3><p>Private tabs are excluded from saved spaces. When a switch would discard private tabs or an unsaved window, Blanc asks you to make an explicit choice.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <aside class="truth-note" aria-labelledby="workspaces-note-title">
    <h2 id="workspaces-note-title">Saved on this device, within this profile.</h2>
    <p>Blanc Spaces are device-local and profile-scoped. They do not sync across devices or move tabs between local profiles. Saving a space preserves its tab setup, not every page’s running state.</p>
    <a class="text-link" href="/support#workspaces" data-track="feature_cta_click" data-feature="named-workspaces" data-cta-position="related-feature">How Blanc Spaces work <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
  </aside>
  <section class="feature-close" aria-labelledby="workspaces-close-title">
    <h2 id="workspaces-close-title">Make room for the way you browse.</h2>
    <a class="cta" href="/download" data-track="feature_cta_click" data-feature="named-workspaces" data-cta-position="feature-close">download blanc</a>
  </section>
</main>
</BaseLayout>
